package fixedwait

// Entry is one function's counted references that the series has not yet
// removed, by the category the survey gave each one.
//
// KEYED BY FUNCTION, NOT BY LINE, so an unrelated edit above a wait never
// churns the table, and COUNTED, so a new wait added beside an old one in
// the same function still fails the gate.
type Entry struct {
	// File is the path from the module's root, slash-separated.
	File string
	// Func is the enclosing top-level declaration as [Ref.Func] names it:
	// a function's name, a method's as Type.Method.
	Func string

	// The deciding categories, the class's three shapes.
	NegativeWindow   int
	HeadStart        int
	PositiveDeadline int
	// ClockStep: the wait only moves the wall clock past an instant the
	// code under test stamped, so that a later stamp differs. It is in the
	// class, since the verdict depends on wall-clock time having passed,
	// though it cannot flake, and no marker takes it out: its fix is a
	// clock the test controls (internal/clocktest, or a Now the code under
	// test is handed), which removes the wait.
	ClockStep int
	// Exempt: the survey read the reference and it decides nothing. The
	// piece that owns it adds the marker, choosing the kind, and re-reads
	// it first: one that turns out to decide a claim is fixed like the
	// deciding ones.
	Exempt int

	// Piece is the number of the series' pull request that removes the
	// entry, in crewlet/crewlet#734's list.
	Piece int
}

// Total is every reference the entry records.
func (e Entry) Total() int {
	return e.NegativeWindow + e.HeadStart + e.PositiveDeadline + e.ClockStep + e.Exempt
}

// allowed is every function whose fixed waits the series has yet to remove.
//
// ADDING AN ENTRY IS THE DECISION, and no piece of the series adds one: the
// table only shrinks. A piece that fixes a function's waits lowers or
// removes its entry in the same diff, and the gate fails an entry that
// records more than its function holds, so a fix cannot leave its entry
// behind. A new wait is decided by one of the house patterns or marked, in
// the package doc.
